# Valgrind suppressions for known, benign false positives in the C++ test suite.
#
# Rayon's global thread pool lazily spawns worker threads on first parallel
# use. The glibc thread-local-storage (TLS) blocks allocated for those
# still-live, detached worker threads are reported by Valgrind as "possibly
# lost" at exit, because the blocks belong to threads the leak checker cannot
# prove are reachable from the main thread's root set. This is not a leak in
# fastlowess — the memory is owned and managed by the runtime/thread teardown.
#
# Only "possible" leaks are suppressed; "definitely lost" and "indirectly
# lost" blocks still fail the run via `--error-exitcode=1`.
{
   rayon-global-threadpool-glibc-TLS
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   ...
   fun:allocate_dtv
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   fun:allocate_stack
   fun:pthread_create*
   ...
}
